{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Living birds.</b> Excludes birds that are tereifah." "<b>Clean birds.</b> Excludes an unclean bird — because skin-afflictions come upon evil speech, which is an act of chattering of words; therefore for his purification he requires birds, which chatter constantly with a chirping sound (Arakhin 16)." "<b>And cedar wood.</b> Because skin-afflictions come upon haughtiness (ibid.)." "<b>And scarlet thread and hyssop.</b> What is his remedy, that he be healed? Let him humble himself from his pride like a worm and like hyssop." "<b>Cedar wood.</b> A rod of cedar." "<b>Scarlet wool.</b> A tongue of wool dyed bright."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:24.150480149Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}